> > > congruency model (Cheung ,2009) "attached" to each of these cfa's, save the
> > >
> > > latent congruence factor scores (which, basically are second-order factors)
> > >
> > > from each of the six models (six waves), and then run a latent growth model
> > >
> > > on the saved factor scores for the latent congruency factors. Following the
> > >
> > > approach suggested by Terrence Jorgensen (use the 10000 estimates per
> > > person -and per wave in my case- as a multiple imputation) is just daunting
> > >
> > > in my case. Would using just the means ("lvmeans") of the 10000 samples
> > > also count as "accounting for the uncertainty"?
> > >
> > > Thank you for your time.
